# Design sequences - PUBLISHED as of 2026-11-03.
#
# These were withheld while each submission window was open. All four windows are
# now closed (EGFR, TNF-alpha, GLP-1R submitted; TfR1 closed 1 Nov unsubmitted), so
# the sequences are published with the write-ups that cite them.
#
# Kept for the record, because the withholding rule was twice written too narrowly:
# it first named each file individually, so a new round2_sequences.csv was not
# covered and got committed; then "submission/challenge2_*" named one challenge, so
# the first challenge 3 file was not covered either. Any future withholding rule
# must match by pattern, not by name.
#
# Challenge 5 (KRAS G12D pMHC) is open until 8 Nov. Its sequences go here, ignored,
# until that window closes.
#
# Caught a third time on 7 Nov, and only because the rule above was read before the
# files existed: the scaffold pipeline writes designed sequences into JSON result
# files, which "submission/challenge5_*" does not cover. Matching by pattern was not
# enough on its own - the patterns also have to cover every PLACE sequences are
# written, not just the submission folder.
pmhc/results/*sequences*.csv
pmhc/results/mpnn_candidates.json
pmhc/results/mpnn_all.json
pmhc/results/specificity.json
submission/challenge5_*

# NOT withheld, and deliberately so: docked_poses.json and shortlist_poses.json carry
# scaffold_seq, which is the Baker lab's already-published scaffold sequence, not ours.

# Downloaded reference structures - re-fetched by the scripts, not source
data/glp1r/

# Docked poses are regenerable from pmhc/dock_scaffolds.py plus the published
# scaffold set (Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.15169815); 151 PDBs is not worth versioning.
data/pmhc/docked/
